+// Suffix of the directory that holds the cache entries, appended to the cache file path the
+// framework hands us. AOSP uses ".multifile". This device uses a different name because
+// Genshin Impact deletes "<cache path>.multifile" every time it starts (seen with kprobes on
+// filename_unlinkat/filename_renameat2: its UnityMain thread renames every entry to *_tmp,
+// unlinks it and removes the directory), which throws away every compiled shader and makes
+// the next session recompile all of them at draw time. It leaves other names alone, including
+// the monolithic cache file at the same path. This is a local workaround, not a fix for
+// upstream: the app is entitled to clear its own cache.
+constexpr char kMultifileDirSuffix[] = ".blobs";
